{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011Cf6hmAdi8sY6nhRs1vaxS","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"<<PHASE:ANALYSIS>>\n\n**Requirement, restated in one sentence:**\nAdd an order cancellation endpoint that transitions active orders to cancelled status, cancels their created shipments with idempotent semantics and all-or-nothing validation, and prevents shipment creation on cancelled orders.\n\n**Repository findings:**\n- Order entity (Order.kt:11-16): No status field\n- OrderController (OrderController.kt:16-46): Has create, getById, list; no cancel\n- OrderRepository (OrderRepository.kt:10-27): In-memory store with save/find/exists methods\n- Shipment entity (Shipment.kt:9-14): Already has ShipmentStatus enum (CREATED, CONFIRMED, CANCELLED)\n- ShipmentController (ShipmentController.kt:22-56): Creates shipments, no order status validation\n- ShipmentRepository (ShipmentRepository.kt:10-27): In-memory store, no findByOrderId\n- Error handling (ApiExceptions.kt:11-25): ResourceNotFoundException (404), ConflictException (409)\n- ErrorCode enum (ApiError.kt:31-37): ORDER_NOT_FOUND, ORDER_ALREADY_EXISTS, SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND, SHIPMENT_ALREADY_EXISTS, VALIDATION_FAILED\n\n**Conventions this repository has:**\n1. Controllers throw ApiException subclasses directly; GlobalExceptionHandler (GlobalExceptionHandler.kt:16-28) converts them to ApiError envelope\n2. Error responses include code, message, and fields in consistent structure\n3. Tests use MockMvc with both status and error envelope assertions\n4. In-memory repositories with thread-safe ConcurrentHashMap\n5. No service layer; business logic in controllers\n6. Kotlin data classes; Spring Boot annotations for dependency injection\n7. @BeforeEach in tests clears repositories\n\n**Affected files:**\n1. Order.kt — must add OrderStatus enum and status field to Order data class\n2. OrderController.kt — must add POST /orders/{orderId}/cancel endpoint\n3. ShipmentRepository.kt — must add findByOrderId method to support shipment lookup\n4. ShipmentController.kt — must inject OrderRepository and validate order status before creating shipment\n5. OrderControllerTest.kt — must add tests for cancel endpoint (active cancel, retry, conflict, 404)\n6. ShipmentControllerTest.kt — may need to add test for shipment creation on cancelled order\n\n**Risks:**\n1. Idempotent semantics: cancelling an already-cancelled order must succeed without error\n2. All-or-nothing: if any shipment is CONFIRMED, entire operation must fail and leave state unchanged\n3. ShipmentController needs access to OrderRepository and must validate order status\n4. Shipment cancellation logic (setting status to CANCELLED on CREATED shipments)\n5. Error code for \"order cancelled\" conflict when creating shipment — can reuse ConflictException\n\n**Open questions:**\nNone identified. Requirement is clear on all cases.\n\n---\n\n<<PHASE:DESIGN>>\n\n**Proposed change, file by file:**\n\n1. **Order.kt**: Add OrderStatus enum (ACTIVE, CANCELLED) and status field to Order. Newly created orders default to ACTIVE.\n\n2. **OrderController.kt**: Add `POST /orders/{orderId}/cancel` endpoint. Logic:\n   - Fetch order by ID; throw 404 ResourceNotFoundException if not found\n   - If already CANCELLED, return 200 with order (idempotent)\n   - Check all shipments for this order; if any is CONFIRMED, throw 409 ConflictException without changing anything\n   - Otherwise, set order status to CANCELLED, cancel all CREATED shipments, save order, return 200 with order\n\n3. **ShipmentRepository.kt**: Add `findByOrderId(orderId: String): List<Shipment>` method to retrieve all shipments for an order.\n\n4. **ShipmentController.kt**: Inject OrderRepository. In create method, before saving shipment, fetch order and check its status. If CANCELLED, throw 409 ConflictException. If order doesn't exist, allow shipment creation (current behavior).\n\n5. **ApiError.kt**: Add error code `ORDER_CANCELLED` for semantic clarity (optional; ConflictException with existing code works).\n\n6. **OrderControllerTest.kt**: Add test cases:\n   - Cancel active order: sets status to CANCELLED, cancels CREATED shipments, returns 200 with order\n   - Retry cancel on cancelled order: succeeds, returns 200, no error\n   - Cancel blocked by CONFIRMED shipment: returns 409, order stays ACTIVE, shipment keeps status\n   - Cancel non-existent order: returns 404\n   \n7. **ShipmentControllerTest.kt**: Add test case:\n   - Create shipment on cancelled order: returns 409\n\n**Alternatives rejected:**\n- **Service layer**: Adding a dedicated OrderService class would be cleaner but violates \"do not modify outside order/shipment features\" constraint and breaks existing pattern. Controllers use repositories directly.\n- **Separate cancel service method in repository**: Putting cancel logic in repository would break the established pattern where repositories are dumb stores and controllers hold business logic.\n- **New error code for cancelled order**: Using ConflictException with ORDER_NOT_FOUND or SHIPMENT_ALREADY_EXISTS reused is possible, but a dedicated ORDER_CANCELLED code is cleaner. However, since the requirement doesn't specify and \"409\" is sufficient, I'll add it for clarity.\n\n**Data and error flow:**\n\n| Case | Flow |\n|------|------|\n| Cancel ACTIVE order with CREATED shipments | Controller finds order (existsById) → checks all shipments (findByOrderId) → none CONFIRMED → sets order.status = CANCELLED → saves order → for each CREATED shipment, sets shipment.status = CANCELLED, saves → returns 200 order |\n| Retry cancel on CANCELLED order | Controller finds order → status already CANCELLED → returns 200 order |\n| Cancel order with CONFIRMED shipment | Controller finds order → checks shipments (findByOrderId) → finds CONFIRMED → throws ConflictException(409) → no state changes (all-or-nothing) |\n| Cancel non-existent order | Controller findById returns null → throws ResourceNotFoundException(404) |\n| Create shipment on CANCELLED order | Controller finds order (existsById) → checks status is CANCELLED → throws ConflictException(409) |\n| Create shipment on non-existent order | Current behavior: order lookup is never done, shipment created anyway |\n\n**Test strategy:**\n\n1. **OrderControllerTest.kt additions:**\n   - `cancels an active order and returns 200` — create order, create CREATED shipment, cancel order, verify order.status = CANCELLED and shipment.status = CANCELLED\n   - `idempotent cancel succeeds and changes nothing` — cancel order, cancel same order again, verify both return 200, status unchanged\n   - `cancel blocked by confirmed shipment returns 409 and changes nothing` — create order, create shipment, confirm shipment (via repository write), cancel order, verify 409, order still ACTIVE, shipment still CONFIRMED\n   - `cancel nonexistent order returns 404` — cancel unknown ID, verify 404 with ORDER_NOT_FOUND code\n\n2. **ShipmentControllerTest.kt additions:**\n   - `creates shipment on nonexistent order` — verify current behavior (no validation) still works\n   - `rejects shipment on cancelled order with 409` — create order, cancel order, try create shipment, verify 409\n\n---\n\n<<PHASE:IMPLEMENTATION>>\n\nNow I'll implement the changes. Starting with Order.kt:"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":879,"cache_read_input_tokens":19182,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":879},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0c2e827d-a35c-4112-a984-0c8b9d98707e","uuid":"ab381c47-cd18-47f7-8bb8-aebcb7f0f673","timestamp":"2026-09-16T07:13:21.449Z","request_id":"req_011Cf6hmABBGRiTSMuoTdTjY"}
